    "label": {},
    "short_label": {
      "en": "$tin_bandlim2"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "$tin_bandlim2 is an annual income threshold used as the Base of the tin_nl/SchedCalc that computes 'Additional income tax (limitation mortgage interest deduction)' — the surcharge that caps mortgage-interest relief below the top marginal rate. Its latest modelled value (€78,426/year) sits just above the Country Report's 'Band2 up to' figure in Table 2.28 (€76,817 in 2025, the point from which the 49.5% top rate applies), consistent with the CR's account of the deduction limitation only biting once income enters the top Box 1 bracket. Per the Country Report, since 2014 the effective mortgage-interest deduction rate for top-bracket taxpayers has been reduced annually via this additional tax (e.g. rising to 12.45% by 2023), and $tin_bandlim2 marks the income level at which this limitation starts to apply."
    },
    "explanation": {
      "en": "EUROMOD function group: Income tax: band_limits"
    },
    "last_confirmed_valid_on": null,
    "temporal_basis": "in_force"
  },
